@startuml 03-contract-state-machine
!theme plain
title Contract State Machine - Event-Driven Transitions with Trigger Sources
footer Sprint 11 Documentation - 2025-12-05

skinparam {
    BackgroundColor white
    StateBackgroundColor #E8E8E8
    StateBorderColor #333333
    NoteBorderColor #333333
}

' Color Legend
legend top left
|= Color |= Source |
|<#90EE90> | Frontend (StripeOrderController) |
|<#87CEEB> | Webhook (WebhookController) |
|<#DDA0DD> | Automatic (Handler Logic) |
|<#FFB6C1> | Terminal State |
endlegend

' State colors by type
skinparam state {
    BackgroundColor<<initial>> #90EE90
    BackgroundColor<<pending>> #90EE90
    BackgroundColor<<ready>> #DDA0DD
    BackgroundColor<<committed>> #90EE90
    BackgroundColor<<fulfilled>> #87CEEB
    BackgroundColor<<terminal>> #FFB6C1
}

state "DRAFT" as Draft <<initial>> {
    Draft : Contract created
    Draft : No conditions fulfilled
    Draft : providerOrderId: null
}

state "PENDING" as Pending <<pending>> {
    Pending : Awaiting conditions
    Pending : payment_authorized added
    Pending : providerOrderId: pi_xxx
}

state "READY_TO_COMMIT" as Ready <<ready>> {
    Ready : All conditions fulfilled
    Ready : Ready to create order
}

state "COMMITTED" as Committed <<committed>> {
    Committed : Order created (OXPAID=0)
    Committed : OXORDERID linked
    Committed : Awaiting webhook
}

state "FULFILLED" as Fulfilled <<fulfilled>> {
    Fulfilled : Payment confirmed
    Fulfilled : OXPAID = NOW()
    Fulfilled : Terminal state
}

state "FAILED" as Failed <<terminal>> {
    Failed : Payment failed
    Failed : failureReason stored
}

state "CANCELLED" as Cancelled <<terminal>> {
    Cancelled : User cancelled
}

state "EXPIRED" as Expired <<terminal>> {
    Expired : Timeout reached
}

' Transitions with trigger sources

[*] --> Draft #Green : <color:green><b>FE</b></color>\n<color:green>StripeOrderController</color>\n<color:green>::createCheckoutSession()</color>

Draft --> Pending #Green : <color:green><b>FE</b></color>\n<color:green>StripeOrderController</color>\n<color:green>::checkoutSuccess()</color>

Pending --> Ready #Purple : <color:purple><b>AUTO</b></color>\n<color:purple>PaymentAuthorizedEventHandler</color>\n<color:purple>areAllConditionsFulfilled()</color>

Ready --> Committed #Green : <color:green><b>FE</b></color>\n<color:green>StripeOrderCreationHandler</color>\n<color:green>::handle()</color>

Committed --> Fulfilled #Blue : <color:blue><b>WEBHOOK</b></color>\n<color:blue>WebhookController::render()</color>\n<color:blue>→ handlePaymentSucceeded()</color>

Committed --> Failed #Blue : <color:blue><b>WEBHOOK</b></color>\n<color:blue>WebhookController::render()</color>\n<color:blue>→ handlePaymentFailed()</color>

Draft --> Cancelled : <color:gray>Not implemented</color>
Pending --> Cancelled : <color:gray>Not implemented</color>
Draft --> Expired : <color:gray>Not implemented</color>
Pending --> Expired : <color:gray>Not implemented</color>

Fulfilled --> [*]
Failed --> [*]
Cancelled --> [*]
Expired --> [*]

' Detailed notes with method chains

note right of Draft #FFFACD
<b>TRIGGER: Frontend</b>
════════════════════════════════════════
<b>Entry Point:</b>
StripeOrderController::createCheckoutSession()

<b>Event Chain:</b>
1. StripeCheckoutSessionRequestEvent dispatched
2. <b>StripeContractCreationHandler::handle()</b>
   → Creates PaymentContract(DRAFT)
   → Saves to osc_payment_contract
3. StripeCheckoutSessionHandler::handle()
   → Creates Stripe Checkout Session
   → Sets providerOrderId on contract

<b>Result:</b>
Contract in DRAFT state
User redirected to Stripe
end note

note right of Pending #FFFACD
<b>TRIGGER: Frontend (Return)</b>
════════════════════════════════════════
<b>Entry Point:</b>
StripeOrderController::checkoutSuccess()

<b>Event Chain:</b>
1. StripeCheckoutReturnEvent dispatched
2. <b>StripeCheckoutReturnHandler::handle()</b>
   → Validates session + token
   → Retrieves Stripe session
   → Dispatches PaymentAuthorizedEvent
3. <b>PaymentAuthorizedEventHandler::handle()</b>
   → contract.transitionToPending()
   → contract.fulfillCondition('payment_authorized')
   → contract.setProvider('stripe', pi_xxx)
   → If all conditions met → READY_TO_COMMIT

<b>Result:</b>
Contract transitions: DRAFT → PENDING → READY_TO_COMMIT
end note

note right of Committed #FFFACD
<b>TRIGGER: Frontend (Continuation)</b>
════════════════════════════════════════
<b>Entry Point:</b>
(Same request as checkoutSuccess)

<b>Event Chain:</b>
1. ContractReadyToCommitEvent dispatched
2. <b>StripeOrderCreationHandler::handle()</b>
   → OxidShopOrderService.createOrder()
   → Order::finalizeOrder()
   → contract.commitToOrder(orderId)
   → ContractCommittedEvent dispatched

<b>Result:</b>
Contract COMMITTED
Order created (OXPAID = '0000-00-00')
User sees thank you page
end note

note right of Fulfilled #E0FFFF
<b>TRIGGER: Webhook</b>
════════════════════════════════════════
<b>Entry Point:</b>
WebhookController::render()
POST /index.php?cl=stripe_webhook

<b>Event Chain:</b>
1. Stripe sends payment_intent.succeeded
2. WebhookProcessingService::processEvent()
3. <b>WebhookContractFulfillmentHandler</b>
   → findByProviderOrderId(pi_xxx)
   → contract.fulfill()
   → ContractFulfilledEvent dispatched
4. updateOrderFieldsAfterContractFulfillment()
   → UPDATE oxorder SET OXPAID = NOW()

<b>Result:</b>
Contract FULFILLED
OXPAID set to current timestamp
end note

note bottom of Failed #FFE4E1
<b>TRIGGER: Webhook</b>
════════════════════════
WebhookController::render()
→ payment_intent.failed
→ handlePaymentFailed()
→ contract.fail(reason)
end note

@enduml
